  "summary": "Malicious code in dolyame-boxy-atom-bnpl-badge (npm)",
  "details": "On require, the package downloads and executes a platform-specific binary payload. It fingerprints the OS/arch, then fetches a binary from Cloudflare Workers endpoints oob-worker[.]cf103-070[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf100-416[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf102-baf[.]workers[.]dev, and oob-worker[.]cf99-9b3[.]workers[.]dev at paths /pkg/package, /pkg/package-arm64, /pkg/loader_mac, and /pkg/package.exe. If HTTPS fetch fails it falls back to a DNS-TXT chunked transfer from c[.]sdk[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru (per-platform hosts sdk[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru, ext[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru, pkg[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru, net[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru). The downloaded binary is written to /tmp/.cache_\u0026lt;hex\u0026gt; (or %TEMP%\\dotnet_diag_\u0026lt;hex\u0026gt;.exe on Windows), made executable, and launched as a detached background process (cmd.exe /c start /b on Windows, /bin/sh -c \u0026lt;path\u0026gt; \u0026amp; on Unix).",
